# With block 0's gates fixed, where is the remaining goal × belief interaction made?

Generated by `gate1.py` (exploratory). The natural network with block 0's gates fixed per goal and step (section 15), 8192 test decisions after the first step, 4096 same-step pairs (posteriors ≥ 0.5 apart). The belief-dependent goal difference of a quantity is (y(h2, B) − y(h2, A)) − (y(h1, B) − y(h1, A)); a route's is the same with the route-swapped state in place of B's, the incoming decision-token residual held at A's. Means over the 12 ordered goal pairs, medians (min–max) over six models.

## 1. The interaction at block 1's input and through block 1

Variance share of the goal × belief interaction beyond a goal × step offset, at the decision token under every goal:

| network | input of block 1 | block-1 attention output | block-1 MLP output | state after block 1 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| natural | 0.06 (0.06–0.07) | 0.07 (0.05–0.10) | 0.15 (0.15–0.18) | 0.10 (0.09–0.13) |
| block-0 gates fixed | 0.03 (0.02–0.03) | 0.05 (0.03–0.08) | 0.11 (0.10–0.14) | 0.06 (0.06–0.09) |

On the same-step pairs, gates fixed: the belief-dependent goal difference is 0.39 (0.38–0.42) of the A-written difference's norm at the input of block 1, 0.64 (0.52–0.74) at block 1's attention output, 0.67 (0.62–0.77) after block 1; R² of the A-written difference for the B-written one 0.83 (0.81–0.84) at the input of block 1, 0.53 (0.37–0.60) after it. The input's belief-dependent difference carried unchanged against the output's: projection 0.19 (0.15–0.24), R² 0.23 (0.17–0.30); the attention output's alone: projection 0.31 (0.26–0.33); input plus attention (the MLP's input): R² 0.54 (0.52–0.56). Block 1's MLP on the belief-dependent difference: a linear map of its input difference across pairs has R² 0.95 (0.94–0.96); gain 1.10 (1.04–1.19).

